# bmkrs engineering rules (applies to bmkrs.com and app.bmkrs.com)

These rules are binding. When a request conflicts with them, follow the rules and say so.

## 1. Match the editorial render

Art direction is locked to the studio moodboard: warm paper field, elegant serif headlines, quiet sans body, terracotta orange CTAs, hairline rules, generous whitespace, magazine pacing.

- Pages open on paper. Prefer paper throughout. Ink and orange are rare accents, not the default canvas.
- Headlines use sentence case (capital first letter). Nav and meta stay lowercase.
- UK English. No em or en dashes. Buttons say what happens ("Talk to us", never "Submit").
- Never ship fabricated people, testimonials, or metrics. Use real CMS/fallback people or leave the slot empty.

## 2. The component library is mandatory

All UI is built from `@bmkrs/ui` (`packages/ui`). Generic shadcn controls may live in `web/src/components/ui` for form chrome only.

- NEVER write a raw styled element when a library component exists. Use `<Button>`, `<Surface>`, `<Kicker>`, `<H1>/<H2>`, `<Body>`, `<Rule>`, `<StorySplit>`, `<TeamGrid>`, `<RuledList>`, `<CategoryTabs>`, `<Sheet>`.
- Missing primitive? Add it to `packages/ui` first, export it, then use it. Do not inline a one-off.

## 3. No hardcoded design values

- NEVER hardcode a colour hex, font family, radius, or spacing in a page or feature component. Use `tokens` / CSS variables from `@bmkrs/ui`.
- Palette: ink `#181613`, paper `#F5F2EB`, orange `#FF4D00`, plus derived body/meta/rule values. No second accent.
- Type trio:
  - Display: Instrument Serif via `--font-display` (weight 400 only, italic allowed)
  - Body / UI: Cabinet Grotesk via `--font-sans` (weights 400 and 500 only)
  - Meta: Fragment/Geist Mono via `--font-mono`
- Archivo is logo SVG only. Never 600/700. Never `font-stretch`, `scaleX`, or tracking tighter than `-0.02em` on display type.

## 4. Surfaces and CTAs

- Every section is a `<Surface theme="ink|paper|orange">`. Colours come from context.
- Default CTA: rectangular orange fill (`--bmkrs-radius-button`). No pills for primary actions.
- Max one full `orange` Surface per page.

## 5. Icons

- Prefer `<StatusDot>`, mono labels, hairline rules, or a simple arrow in the button label.
- No icon library (lucide, heroicons, etc.) without explicit human approval.

## 6. Accessibility

- Tap targets >= 44px. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Forms: real labels, orange focus rings, 16px input text minimum.

## 7. When unsure

State which library component you are using and why. If you cannot do it within these rules, say what is missing rather than working around them.
